    "source": "glen-park-context-statement",
    "note": "Named with 131 Brompton Avenue as one of the small wood-frame cottages with a gabled roof and bay windows that the G. H. Umbsden Realty Company supplied with the tract lots it marketed after 1906, for ten per cent down and $10 a month. Recorded in the reconnaissance survey of 110 parcels but not evaluated individually; buildings the evaluation did not evaluate are treated as potential historical resources pending further project-level study."
